: Calculate the i-th Fibonacci number.

: -01-          i

: a in M/X      Larger number in the sequence.
: b in R1       Smaller number in the sequence.
: i in M/X      Remaining loops.

01  C           : Clear display.
02  STO
03   [1]        : 0->b, Initialize the smaller number to be 0.
04  1
05  MIN         : 1->i, Initialize the larger number to be 1.
06  ENT         : i, Index of the Fibonacci number.
07  GOTO [6]    : Jump into the loop. A jump to the decrementing step is made
                : as the entered index is one larger than desired.
08. X-M         : i'->M, a->X, Put the index away, get the larger number out.
09  +
10  X-S
11   [1]        : a->b', b->X, The larger number now will be the new small.
12  =           : a + b, Calculate the next number in the sequence.
13  X-M         : a'->M, i->X, Put the result away, get the index out.
14. -           : Loop is entered here.
15  1
16  =           : i - 1, Decrement the index.
17  X>0 [-9]    : Jump if the index is still positive.
18  X-M         : a->X, Display the resulting larger number.
